invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_parser.c
catches: handshake_strict_webpki
reason: the ALPN arm admits a ProtocolName of zero bytes, which RFC 7301
  §3.1 puts outside the 1..255 range a ProtocolName takes. The empty
  name matches no offered protocol, so the session fails with
  illegal_parameter instead of the decode_error RFC 9846 §6 names for a
  length out of range, and the wire alert names the wrong fault.
  bin/handshake_strict_webpki's empty-name row objects.

--- old
    if (e.err || name_len == 0 || list_len != 1 + name_len || rb_left(&e) != 0) {
--- new
    if (e.err || list_len != 1 + name_len || rb_left(&e) != 0) {
